From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable USB0 as a USB
 gadget

The Type-C port J16 is the 5 V input of the board and the only port of
USB0. It has no VBUS supply and no ID or VBUS detect line to the SoC,
so it can only be a peripheral; without a detect line the PHY driver
reports VBUS as present.

Enable the OTG controller in peripheral mode. The EHCI and OHCI of USB0
stay disabled.

Not covered: the USB-C port J4, which is a USB 3 host.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted; with J16 on a host, a composite
gadget (ACM, NCM, mass storage) enumerates at high speed after a cold
start, also with the plug turned over.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 761ca15eab41..61ecb941a82a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -525,6 +525,16 @@ &usb3_u2phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usb_otg {
+	/*
+	 * The Type-C port J16 is the board's 5 V input: it has no VBUS
+	 * supply of its own and no ID or VBUS detect line to the SoC.
+	 * Use the controller as a peripheral only.
+	 */
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &usbphy {
 	usb1_vbus-supply = <&reg_usb1_vbus>;
 	status = "okay";
